Package: uzunyx-deco
Version: @VERSION@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: emi <285864120+antarest47@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: kwin-style-aurorae (>= 6.7), kwin-wayland (>= 4:6.7), qml6-module-qtquick-effects (>= 6.9), qml6-module-org-kde-kirigami
Conflicts: waifbian-deco
Replaces: waifbian-deco
Description: rounded KWin window decoration that stays rounded when maximized
 QML window decoration for the KWin Aurorae engine with 8px rounded
 corners, thin borders, shadows and glossy black minimize, maximize (also
 used for restore) and close buttons (white, and red for close). Unlike Breeze it keeps its borders and
 rounded corners on maximized windows, so maximized windows stay truly
 maximized (with a working restore button) and still look rounded.
 .
 Select it in System Settings > Colors & Themes > Window Decorations, or
 install uzunyx-lookandfeel, whose global theme uses it.
 .
 Also ships the "Soft maximize" KWin script, enabled by default: windows
 that draw their own frame (Firefox, Electron, libadwaita apps) stay
 normal windows filling the maximize area when maximized, so they keep
 their own rounded corners. Their maximize button keeps showing
 "maximize".
 .
 Alt+Tab uses its own switcher in the style of Cover Switch, with live previews.
 /etc/xdg/kwinrc enables KWin's "magic lamp" minimize animation instead of
 "squash", lasting 300 ms like macOS (KWin's default is 250 ms).
